<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wallia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 415–<a href="/years/418">418</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wallia was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> from 415 to 418. After a failed attempt to cross to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, he made peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, returned the captive Galla Placidia and fought for the empire in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a>, destroying the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siling-vandals">Siling Vandals</a> and crushing the Alans. In 418 Rome rewarded the Visigoths with settlement as federates in Aquitaine, where his successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-i">Theodoric I</a> founded the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wallia.jpg" alt="Wallia" width="320" height="521" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alejo Vera · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Walia,_rey_de_los_Visigodos_(Museo_del_Prado).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 418 Honorius rewarded his federates under King <b>Wallia</b> (415–418) with land in the Garonne valley of Gallia Aquitania.</blockquote><a href="/empire/visigothic-kingdom">Visigothic Kingdom · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>From 416 the Visigothic king <b>Wallia</b>, acting for Rome, campaigned against them, and in 418 Addax was killed.</blockquote><a href="/state/alan-kingdom-in-hispania">Alan Kingdom in Hispania</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=43.6,1.44&amp;year=416" aria-label="Toulouse on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4585 618 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Wallia"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5035 888h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5035 888h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=43.6,1.44&amp;year=416">What was here in 416 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
